// scripts/streak-source.mjs - the AUTHORED source for the Streak bank beyond
// day 61. Build it with:
//
//   node scripts/gen-streak.mjs && node scripts/verify-streak.mjs
//
// WHAT LIVES HERE AND WHAT DOES NOT. Only the writing: the question, its true
// answer, and three wrong answers, in that order. The ids, the correct answer's
// column, the order the four choices are printed in, the quizId, the dateLabel
// and the calendar all belong to scripts/gen-streak.mjs and must never be
// typed here. In particular there is no `correct` index in this file at all,
// which is the point: a bank whose author picks the position drifts into a
// column bias inside a month, and days 1..61 (authored by hand, before this
// file existed) are the reason the generator exists.
//
// DAYS 1..61 ARE NOT IN THIS FILE. They shipped hand-written and are frozen
// history; the generator only ever rebuilds ids from FIRST_DAY up. Do not
// backfill them here to "tidy up" - that would rewrite boards players have
// already seen, and the generator refuses to write if the frozen prefix of
// either shipped file moves by a byte.
//
// SHAPE OF A DAY. Exactly 40 entries, tier-major and lane-minor: slots 1-8 are
// tier 1 in LANES order, slots 9-16 tier 2 in LANES order, and so on to tier 5.
// The generator throws if a slot's tier or lane is out of step, so a misplaced
// entry cannot silently shift the whole day by one.
//
// AUTHORING RULES, all of them enforced by scripts/verify-streak.mjs except the
// first two, which stay human jobs:
//
//   1. EVERY FACT IS TRUE AND CHECKABLE. Written and checked at authoring time
//      (2026-09-05).
//   2. THE TIER IS A PROMISE. Tier 1 is "everybody knows this", tier 5 is
//      "a specialist knows this" - the client prints them as Warm-up, Easy,
//      Medium, Hard and Brutal above the question, and a tier-5 gimme is a
//      broken promise even though no script can catch it.
//   3. NOTHING THAT EXPIRES. Never ask who holds a post, a title or a record
//      now. Pin every fact to a year, a decade or an event: not "who has won
//      the most Grand Slam titles" but "who completed the first Grand Slam in
//      1938". The verifier fails the time-relative wording that marks the
//      unpinned version ("currently", "as of", "so far", "to date", "the
//      reigning", "holds the record").
//   4. THE STEM NEVER HANDS OVER THE ANSWER, whole or in all of its
//      distinctive words.
//   5. US SPELLINGS in everything a reader sees. Authored trivia copy defaults
//      to British forms - theatre, colour, metre, travelling, grey - and the
//      shared screen in scripts/us-spellings.mjs is what stops them. A real
//      title keeps its own spelling and goes on ALLOW_PROPER in
//      scripts/streak-rules.mjs, never silenced in the copy.
//   6. POOL VARIETY ACROSS THE WHOLE WINDOW. No answer may be correct more
//      than four times in days 62.. , counted over every day at once and not
//      per day. Days 1..61 answer "four" 16 times, "China" 10 times and
//      "France" 8, and every per-day check they had was green the whole time.
//   7. THREE PLAUSIBLE DISTRACTORS. Same kind of thing as the answer, same
//      register, same rough length. Three countries, or three composers, or
//      three years - never two countries and a joke.
//   8. NO DOUBLE QUOTES IN COPY. The shipped file emits single-quoted JS
//      strings; write inner quotation with apostrophes instead. No em dashes
//      either: the site's writing rules ban them outright.
//
//   9. AT MOST ONE SPORTS RULES-TYPE QUESTION A DAY (owner ruling,
//      2026-09-23). A Sports slot that asks how a sport works (points for a
//      score, how many players or periods, what a play, term, violation or
//      position is called, officials, equipment, or which sport fits a
//      description of its mechanics) may appear once a day at most; spend the
//      other four on a sport's history, people, teams, records and events.
//      Checked by scripts/sports-rules-classifier.mjs via verify-streak.mjs.
//
// WHERE THE RUNWAY ENDS. The binding constraint is not the calendar, it is
// tier 1 and tier 2 in the eight lanes: a genuine warm-up question has to be
// something almost everyone knows, and the stock of those is finite and already
// 61 days spent. Tiers 3 to 5 have far more room. If a future extension starts
// pushing tier-2 material up into tier 1 to fill slots, stop and shorten the
// run instead - the ramp is the game.
